    <string name="pif_footer_body">A Canary fingerprint is checked at most once a day and replaced automatically once it is within about two weeks of expiring. Canary configs expire roughly 6 weeks from their release date — the expiry is shown in the active config summary.\n\nFor manual setup:\n1. Tap "Fetch Pixel Canary fingerprint" and select a device.\n2. If no devices are found, import a working PIF config from a trusted source. Config files are not provided.\n3. Recheck your Play Integrity status.\n\nAlways delete the active configuration before importing a new one. Loading an expired PIF config will cause TrickyStore strong integrity to fail even with a valid keybox.\n\nAdvanced spoofing:\n• Play Store fingerprint spoof — leave disabled unless advised otherwise. Spoofing FINGERPRINT to Play Store is rarely needed and may cause issues.\n• Spoof SDK to Play Store — presents SDK 32 to the Play Store to force the legacy pre-Android 13 verdict path. It can break Play Store behavior, so leave it off unless testing.\n• Spoof build fields and system properties — leave on. They present the fingerprint to DroidGuard.\n• Spoof keystore provider — keep off when a keybox is in use, since it bypasses keybox attestation.\n• Spoof ROM signature — experimental.</string>
